# Architecture Rules

## Before writing code

1. Search the repo for an existing module.
2. Check Shared Core, Education Core, Monetization Core, Media Core.
3. Reuse or extend — do not duplicate.
4. Prefer ports/adapters for providers.
5. Update docs when boundaries change.

## Dependency direction

Apps → Education/Monetization/Media cores → Shared Core → infrastructure ports.

Never invert. Never copy Shared Core into an app.

## Forbidden

- Duplicate Auth, Payment, Entitlement, Ads/Reward, Analytics, Security, Storage client, API error handling, Design System
- Hard-coding a single cloud/payment/ads/AI provider into domain logic
- Architecture changes that block multi-app or marketplace evolution without explicit approval

## Ambiguity

If a change affects database, payment, entitlement, security, video, or access policy — do not silently pick a high-impact option; surface the conflict.
